WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.112
Random numbers are useful for simulations, experiments, sampling, and creating test data.

00:00:07.112 --> 00:00:11.607
Modern NumPy recommends using its generator interface.

00:00:11.607 --> 00:00:15.912
In code, you will often see the default RNG function.

00:00:16.771 --> 00:00:20.903
A seed lets us reproduce the same sequence of random values.

00:00:20.903 --> 00:00:29.073
Reproducibility is important because it allows someone else to run the same analysis and obtain the same simulated data.

00:00:29.073 --> 00:00:35.988
In a classroom example, a fixed seed also means everyone can compare results more easily.

00:00:35.988 --> 00:00:41.603
Remember that setting a seed does not make the values non-random in a statistical sense;

00:00:41.603 --> 00:00:44.548
it simply makes the generated sequence repeatable.
